text:
Cellulitis of the lower extremity managed with insulin sliding scale;
Patient remained stable on general surgery service on day 5;
Patient monitored on general surgery service and remained hemodynamically stable.

- Patient managed for acute pancreatitis with anticoagulation with apixaban;
- Remained stable on general surgery service on day 4;
- Monitored on general surgery service;
- Remained hemodynamically stable.

- Patient managed for hypertensive crisis with antihypertensive titration;
- Patient remained stable on gastroenterology service on day 6;
- Patient monitored on gastroenterology service;
- Patient remained hemodynamically stable.

- Chronic kidney disease stage 3 with cholecystectomy continued to be managed;
- Remained stable on the infectious disease service on day 6;
- Continued to be monitored on the infectious disease service;
- Remained hemodynamically stable.

- Acute pancreatitis ongoing; managed with laparoscopic appendectomy;
- Day 8: patient remained stable on critical care service;
- Patient monitored on critical care service;
- Patient remained hemodynamically stable.

Patient managed for sepsis secondary to UTI with narrowed ceftriaxone monotherapy;
Patient remained stable on general surgery service on day 10;
Patient monitored on general surgery service;
Patient remained hemodynamically stable.

- Chronic kidney disease stage 3 managed with fluid resuscitation; patient remained stable on the neurology service on day 7;
- Patient monitored on the neurology service;
- Patient remained hemodynamically stable.
